<title>FINLAND: ETLA sees quicker Finnish growth, slow inflation.</title>
<headline>ETLA sees quicker Finnish growth, slow inflation.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish GDP growth will accelerate to four percent this year and ease slightly to 3.5 percent in 1998, while inflation stays subdued, a domestic economic think-tank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;GDP will grow this year by four percent and next year by 3.5 percent,&quot; the Research Institute of the Finnish Economy (ETLA) said in a summary of its 1997/1 forecast.</p>
<p>&quot;Inflation will remain in check,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>&quot;The Finnish economy is rebuilding momentum after a slowdown in growth lasting about one year,&quot; ETLA said, adding: &quot;...there is little danger of the economy overheating in the near future.&quot;</p>
<p>Key figures in ETLA's March 19, 1997 forecast:</p>
<p>			   1996	 1997	  1998</p>
<p> GDP		     +3.2	   +4	  +3.5</p>
<p> Exports (goods)     +4.6	   +6	  +5.5</p>
<p> Imports (goods)     +8.4	   +7	    +6</p>
<p> Consumption	   +3.4	   +3	    +3</p>
<p>  --private	    +3.5	   +4	    +3</p>
<p>  --public	     +2.9	   +1	    +2</p>
<p> Investment	    +5.3	   +9	    +5</p>
<p>  --private	    +6.4	   +9	    +4</p>
<p>  --public	     +0.1	  +10	  +7.5</p>
<p> Industrial output   +3.4	   +6	    +5</p>
<p> CPI		     +0.6	 +1.0	  +1.7</p>
<p> Wage level	    +3.9	   +3	  +3.5</p>
<p> Unemployment	  15.7	 14.6	  13.6</p>
<p> C/A, pct of GDP     +3.4	   +3	    +3</p>
<p>*Public sector deficit,</p>
<p> pct of GDP	     2.6	  1.5	     1</p>
<p>*Public sector gross debt,</p>
<p> pct of GDP	    58.8	   57	    55</p>
<p> 3-mth Helibor	  3.6	    3	   3.5 @</p>
<p>NOTE - * relevant for third stage of economic and monetary union (EMU), which Finland wants to join from its scheduled start in 1999.</p>
